# text = Miss Matilda Jenkyns ( who did not mind being called Miss Matty , when Miss Jenkyns was not by ) wrote nice , kind , rambling letters , now and then venturing into an opinion of her own ; but suddenly pulling herself up , and either begging me not to name what she had said , as Deborah thought differently , and SHE knew , or else putting in a postscript to the effect that , since writing the above , she had been talking over the subject with Deborah , and was quite convinced that , etc .--( here probably followed a recantation of every opinion she had given in the letter ).
