# text = Miss Matty humbly apologised for writing at the same time as her sister , who was so much more capable than she to describe the honour done to Cranford ; but in spite of a little bad spelling , Miss Matty's account gave me the best idea of the commotion occasioned by his lordship's visit , after it had occurred ; for , except the people at the Angel , the Browns , Mrs Jamieson , and a little lad his lordship had sworn at for driving a dirty hoop against the aristocratic legs , I could not hear of any one with whom his lordship had held conversation .
