# text = The evening of the day on which we heard of Mr Holbrook's death , Miss Matilda was very silent and thoughtful ; after prayers she called Martha back and then she stood uncertain what to say she said , at last and then she made so long a pause that Martha , to remind her of her half-finished sentence , dropped a curtsey , and said said she in a low voice She spoke as if she were providing for some distant contingency , and was rather startled when Martha made her ready eager answer Though Miss Matty was startled , she submitted to Fate and Love I have often noticed that almost every one has his own individual small economies -- careful habits of saving fractions of pennies in some one peculiar direction -- any disturbance of which annoys him more than spending shillings or pounds on some real extravagance .
