# text = Another tray thought I For Miss Barker had ordered ( nay , I doubt not , prepared , although she did say and looked pleasantly surprised at the unexpected pleasure ) all sorts of good things for supper -- scalloped oysters , potted lobsters , jelly , a dish called " little Cupids " ( which was in great favour with the Cranford ladies , although too expensive to be given , except on solemn and state occasions -- macaroons sopped in brandy , I should have called it , if I had not known its more refined and classical name ).
