# text = Really I do not know how much was true or false in the reports which flew about like wildfire just at this time ; but it seemed to me then that there was every reason to believe that at Mardon ( a small town about eight miles from Cranford ) houses and shops were entered by holes made in the walls , the bricks being silently carried away in the dead of the night , and all done so quietly that no sound was heard either in or out of the house .
