# text = We were thankful , as Miss Pole desired us to be , that we had never been married ; but I think , of the two , we were even more thankful that the robbers had left Cranford ; at least I judge so from a speech of Miss Matty's that evening , as we sat over the fire , in which she evidently looked upon a husband as a great protector against thieves , burglars , and ghosts ; and said that she did not think that she should dare to be always warning young people against matrimony , as Miss Pole did continually ; to be sure , marriage was a risk , as she saw , now she had had some experience ; but she remembered the time when she had looked forward to being married as much as any one said she , hastily checking herself up , as if she were afraid of having admitted too much
