# text = Mr Hoggins looked broad and radiant , and creaked up the middle aisle at church in a brand-new pair of top-boots -- an audible , as well as visible , sign of his purposed change of state ; for the tradition went , that the boots he had worn till now were the identical pair in which he first set out on his rounds in Cranford twenty-five years ago ; only they had been new-pieced , high and low , top and bottom , heel and sole , black leather and brown leather , more times than any one could tell .
